## 5) Prepared statements + parameters (don’t do f-strings)

### Cypher parameter syntax

Parameters are marked with `$` (e.g., `$min_age`). ([Kuzu][6])

### Python API: pass parameters as a dictionary

```python
min_age, max_age = 18, 30

conn.execute("""
    MATCH (p:Person)
    WHERE p.age > $min_age AND p.age < $max_age
    RETURN p.name;
""", parameters={"min_age": min_age, "max_age": max_age})
```

This is explicitly documented as the recommended approach (and string interpolation is discouraged). ([Kuzu][6])

