## 8) On-disk storage: single-file DB + WAL/shadow/tmp files

### Single-file format (since 0.11.0)

Kuzu switched to a **single-file database format** starting in version **0.11.0** (previously it used a directory). ([Kuzu][8])

### What files exist and why

Kuzu documents these file types (created alongside the main DB file):

* `example.kuzu` — persistent data valid as of last checkpoint
* `example.kuzu.wal` — records updates since last checkpoint; removed after successful checkpoint
* `example.kuzu.shadow` — created during checkpoint; removed after success
* `example.kuzu.tmp` — used to **spill intermediate data** to disk under high memory pressure; removed after the query finishes ([Kuzu][8])

This is **very “analytical DB” flavored**: spill-to-disk for intermediates is a classic operator/execution engine behavior. ([Kuzu][8])

